/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Filters_SingleRate Single-rate filters
 * @ingroup DspCore_Filters
 * @brief Filters whose input and output advance at the same sample rate.
 *
 * `FIR` and `IIR` are SISO, causal, block-processing implementations. Both
 * retain only algorithmic delay state and consume caller-owned
 * Processing::SampleBlock views. They do not own streams, route channels, or
 * manage an audio clock.
 *
 * - FIR implements a finite numerator polynomial and a finite impulse
 *   response.
 * - IIR implements a rational transfer function with numerator and
 *   denominator polynomials.
 * - Biquad designs a second-order IIR coefficient set that IIR can consume.
 */
